```

### 5.5 ComboChart

```tsx
<ComboChart
  dataset={dataset}
  mapping={{
    x: "date",
    series: [
      { y: "volume_kg",   type: "bar",  label: "Volume",    aggregation: "sum" },
      { y: "intensity",   type: "line", label: "Intensity", aggregation: "avg" },
    ]
  }}
  options={{ title: "Volume & Intensity" }}
/>

// Dual axis variant:
series: [
  { y: "volume_kg", type: "bar",  y_axis: "left",  aggregation: "sum" },
  { y: "intensity", type: "line", y_axis: "right", aggregation: "avg" },
]
```

### 5.6 ErrorCard

```tsx
<ErrorCard error={apiError} />
// Rendered automatically by TableView, BarChart, LineChart, ComboChart on ApiError.
// Also available standalone.
// Shows: error.message (prominent) + collapsible error.detail + request_id
```

### 5.7 WarningPlaceholder

```tsx
<WarningPlaceholder
  reason="bar_mode requires group_by"
  suggestion="Add group_by: 'athlete' to the mapping, or remove bar_mode"
  config={invalidMappingObject}   // attached to DebugPanel log
/>
// Never dismissible. Always explains why and suggests the fix.
```

### 5.8 CreateForm

Generic form primitive for creating a new entity. The application declares its fields; `CreateForm` renders the right input type for each and manages submission lifecycle.

```tsx
import CreateForm from "../components/CreateForm";
import type { FormField } from "../api/types";

const FIELDS: FormField[] = [
  { key: "title",       label: "Title",       type: "string", required: true,  placeholder: "Task title" },
  { key: "description", label: "Description", type: "string" },
  { key: "priority",    label: "Priority",    type: "enum",   required: true,
    options: [
      { value: "low",    label: "Low" },
      { value: "medium", label: "Medium" },
      { value: "high",   label: "High" },
    ]
  },
  { key: "due_date", label: "Due Date", type: "date" },
];

<CreateForm
  title="New Task"
  fields={FIELDS}
  submitLabel="Create"            // optional, default: "Create"
  onCancel={() => setCreating(false)}
  onSubmit={async (data) => {
    const res = await apiFetch<Dataset>("/tasks", {
      method: "POST",
      body:   JSON.stringify(data),
    });
    if (isApiError(res)) return res;  // CreateForm renders ErrorCard
    setDataset(res);
    setCreating(false);
  }}
/>
```

**Field type → input mapping:**

| `FormField.type` | Rendered input |
|---|---|
| `"string"` | `<input type="text">` |
| `"number"` | `<input type="number">` |
| `"date"` | `<input type="date">` (native, not M3 Date Picker — see UI_DesignLanguage §10) |
| `"enum"` | `<select>` — `options` is required |
| `"boolean"` | `<select>` with Yes / No options |

**Rules:**
- `onSubmit` receives `Record<string, unknown>` — empty fields are `null`.
- If `onSubmit` returns an `ApiError`, `ErrorCard` is rendered inside the form.
- `CreateForm` never resets on error — the user can correct and retry.
- Do not add validation beyond `required` in the UI — backend validates and returns `ApiError`.

